WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.745
Henry gasped. "Jill took the baseball glove!" he said.

2
00:00:07.746 --> 00:00:10.262
"She must be the barn thief!"

3
00:00:10.263 --> 00:00:14.638
"Let's get your glove back before she hides it somewhere," Cole said.

4
00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:17.840
Both boys jumped out of their hiding place.

5
00:00:17.841 --> 00:00:21.520
Jill had already disappeared around the corner.

6
00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.567
But they could hear her calling Maggie's name.

7
00:00:24.568 --> 00:00:30.453
"That's weird," said Henry. "Why is she yelling for Maggie?"

8
00:00:30.454 --> 00:00:34.777
He ran toward Big Spot's stall with Cole right behind him.

9
00:00:34.778 --> 00:00:40.196
They got there just in time to see Jill handing Henry's baseball glove to Maggie.

10
00:00:40.197 --> 00:00:44.212
"I found this lying on the floor," Jill said with a frown.

11
00:00:44.213 --> 00:00:47.626
"I assume it belongs to your cousin or his friend.

12
00:00:47.627 --> 00:00:51.355
You'd better tell them that this is a barn, not a baseball field."

13
00:00:51.356 --> 00:00:56.788
"You can tell them yourself," Maggie said. "They're right behind you."

14
00:00:56.789 --> 00:01:01.635
"Oh!" Jill spun around and saw Henry and Cole.

15
00:01:01.636 --> 00:01:04.411
"Does this glove belong to one of you?

16
00:01:04.412 --> 00:01:08.694
Because I have enough to do around here without picking up after visitors."

17
00:01:08.695 --> 00:01:13.497
"It's mine," Henry said. "Sorry about that."

18
00:01:13.498 --> 00:01:20.533
"That's okay." Jill shrugged. "Just don't do it again, okay?"

19
00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:26.569
"Oh well," Cole said after she was gone. "That plan didn't work."

20
00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.737
Maggie looked worried.

21
00:01:28.738 --> 00:01:32.776
"You'd better hurry and figure out a better plan," she said.

22
00:01:32.777 --> 00:01:36.928
"It's already time for my lesson to start."

23
00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:41.701
She led Big Spot out of his stall and down the aisle toward the riding ring.

24
00:01:41.702 --> 00:01:45.161
"Maybe we should watch the lesson," Cole said.

25
00:01:45.162 --> 00:01:50.400
"It doesn't seem like Jill is the thief. Or Zach or Eleanor.

26
00:01:50.401 --> 00:01:53.626
That means we need to watch Daisy."

27
00:01:53.627 --> 00:02:00.481
"Okay. I guess it's safe to leave my glove here since nobody seems to want to steal it," Henry said.

28
00:02:00.482 --> 00:02:05.811
"But should we take Maggie's stuff with us?" He picked up the bag.

29
00:02:05.812 --> 00:02:08.727
"I don't want anything else to get stolen."

30
00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:14.897
Cole sneezed. "No way! Put that down," he said.

31
00:02:14.898 --> 00:02:18.983
"Cat hair flies out of it every time you touch it.

32
00:02:18.984 --> 00:02:21.832
Maggie must have let her kittens sleep in it."

33
00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:25.886
"Probably." Henry set the bag down.

34
00:02:25.887 --> 00:02:29.760
"Aunt Ellen says the kittens get into everything."

35
00:02:29.761 --> 00:02:36.526
"I can tell." Cole pointed to the bag. "Look, isn't that a cat toy?"

36
00:02:36.527 --> 00:02:43.486
"Yes." Henry laughed and grabbed the mouse-shaped toy.

37
00:02:43.487 --> 00:02:48.382
"The kittens probably batted it inside, and Maggie didn't notice.

38
00:02:48.383 --> 00:02:53.005
I'd better stick it in the bottom of the bag so the barn cat doesn't grab it."

39
00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:58.943
"Yeah." Cole grinned. "That's all we need—another thief!"

40
00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:04.911
Leaving the bag behind, the boys headed outside to watch the lesson.

41
00:03:04.912 --> 00:03:09.717
They were halfway to the riding ring when Little Spot ran over to them.

42
00:03:09.718 --> 00:03:14.091
"Hi, Little Spot," Cole said, rubbing the beagle's ears.

43
00:03:14.092 --> 00:03:16.657
Henry was looking at the ring.

44
00:03:16.658 --> 00:03:20.943
Ms. Wood was in the center with three riders trotting around her.

45
00:03:20.944 --> 00:03:24.887
"It looks like Daisy isn't here today," Henry said.

46
00:03:24.888 --> 00:03:30.002
"Really?" Cole stopped petting Little Spot and stood up.

47
00:03:30.003 --> 00:03:33.924
"That means if she's the thief, nothing will disappear today."

48
00:03:33.925 --> 00:03:40.366
Henry nodded. "Right! That could be why my glove . . ."

49
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:43.731
He stopped talking in the middle of his sentence.

50
00:03:43.732 --> 00:03:47.859
Eleanor had jumped down from her pony and run out the gate.

51
00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:51.904
She had almost reached the area where the boys were standing.

52
00:03:51.905 --> 00:03:55.133
"Are you okay?" Henry called to her.

53
00:03:55.134 --> 00:04:01.510
"I'm fine," Eleanor said. "I just need to go inside and get a tissue."

54
00:04:01.511 --> 00:04:04.359
She raced past, heading for the barn.

55
00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.672
Little Spot barked and ran after his owner.

56
00:04:07.673 --> 00:04:10.207
"That's weird," Cole said.

57
00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:14.162
"Couldn't she wait until the end of the lesson to get a tissue?

58
00:04:14.163 --> 00:04:17.977
That could be suspicious behavior."

59
00:04:17.978 --> 00:04:20.603
"Maybe," Henry said.

60
00:04:20.604 --> 00:04:25.578
"But Eleanor is always complaining about how hard she's working, remember?

61
00:04:25.579 --> 00:04:30.448
Maybe she just used the tissue story as an excuse to take a break."

62
00:04:30.449 --> 00:04:34.870
"Oh yeah." Cole shrugged. "You're probably right."

63
00:04:34.871 --> 00:04:38.937
Henry and Cole walked the rest of the way to the ring.

64
00:04:38.938 --> 00:04:43.813
Maggie and Zach were still riding while Ms. Wood watched and gave them tips.

65
00:04:43.814 --> 00:04:47.045
A few minutes later, Eleanor came out of the barn.

66
00:04:47.046 --> 00:04:53.160
Soon she was back on her pony.

67
00:04:53.161 --> 00:04:57.069
When the lesson ended, Maggie led her pony over to the boys.

68
00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:01.251
"Did you solve the mystery yet?" she asked them.

69
00:05:01.252 --> 00:05:07.209
"Not yet," Henry said. "But we noticed Daisy is absent.

70
00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:11.024
If she's the thief, nothing will get stolen today."

71
00:05:11.025 --> 00:05:15.242
"Oh! Good point." Maggie nodded.

72
00:05:15.243 --> 00:05:18.175
"You just have to figure out a way to prove it."

73
00:05:18.176 --> 00:05:21.514
"Don't worry, we will," said Henry.

74
00:05:21.515 --> 00:05:26.382
"Okay." Maggie didn't look too sure about that.

75
00:05:26.383 --> 00:05:33.043
Just then Eleanor led her pony up to them, so The Lemonade Detectives had to stop discussing the case.

76
00:05:33.044 --> 00:05:35.473
They all walked into the barn.

77
00:05:35.474 --> 00:05:40.655
Maggie led Spot into his stall, and then turned to put her riding helmet in her bag.

78
00:05:40.656 --> 00:05:44.325
As soon as she leaned over, she let out a shriek.

79
00:05:44.326 --> 00:05:54.550
"I can't believe this!" she yelled. "One of my sandals is gone!"

